{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-logging-county snapshot tables",
    "description": "A SOURCE-CATALOG FILE (esm-spec §2): data_sources only, no component, not mountable as a subsystem. It declares every snapshot table the nr-logging-county chain reads -- twenty-six entries covering all seven stages of PLAN.md §3 Phase 2 -- so that the ingest configuration is written, reviewed and version-controlled before it can be run, rather than invented under time pressure on the day it can.\n\nNOTHING CONSUMES IT YET, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. No CLI subcommand can load a data source at the pinned toolchain: `src/bin/esm.rs` supplies no PrepareProvider, so a parameter with `update.kind: \"data\"` silently keeps its default and an aggregate over it silently sums to zero (build-esm.sh, KNOWN BLOCKER; PLAN.md §1.5). Wiring a component to one of these entries today would make a green test that compared nothing. THE SHAPE IS THE RUNTIME'S, NOT THE SCHEMA'S GUESS: the format is `metadata.esio_format`, because a `format` key inside `reader_options` is rejected as an unknown reader option (esm-spec §8.9.1 working as specified), and `url_template` carries an explicit `file://` scheme, because a bare absolute path fails with a missing-scheme error. Both were found by building the in-flight provider and running the real ingest. So the entries are declared and CHECKED -- tools/check-sources.py opens every file named here with pyarrow and verifies that it exists, that every `float_columns` entry is really a column, that none of them is already a float, and that no projected decimal-text column was left out -- while the components read `const` arrays transcribed from these same tables.\n\nWHAT IT ALREADY PROVES: that `float_columns` is mandatory, and on almost every table rather than only on MOVESOutput. Checked directly against the parquet: `surrogatequant`, `population`, `fractionLifeused`, `percentageScrapped`, `NREngTechFraction`, `monthFraction`, `dayFraction`, `marketShare`, all seventeen `fuelformulation` property columns, `zonemonthhour.temperature`, `nrsourceusetype`'s four activity columns, `nremissionrate.meanBaseRate`, `nrdeterioration.DFCoefficient` and `MOVESOutput.emissionQuant` are all physically `string` in the file, holding decimal text for byte-reproducibility, even where the sidecar .meta.json calls them float64. Without `float_columns` they arrive as strings and no arithmetic on them means anything. Two traps the catalog also records: `nrscrappagecurve.fractionLifeused` is spelled with a lowercase u, and `nrdayallocation.scc` is lowercase throughout.\n\nWHAT AGEDIST'S FOLD COSTS, AND WHAT IS NOW COMPUTED INSTEAD OF CARRIED. Every input the fold consumes comes out of the snapshot now: the 197-row `nrscrappagecurve` step lookup, the year-over-year scrapped fractions, `nyrlif`, the sales curve, the base model-year fractions, and getgrw's whole indicator series with the thirty annual `grwfac` factors it implies -- exact table rows, an interpolated year, and a year-over-year DIP whose negative factor is the mechanism §6.3 calls the most fragile behaviour in the chain. §7.3's 5.9604645e-08 age-3 survival is computed here too, which is the first time this fixture has asserted anything about it rather than receiving it inside a constant. What is still carried is the fold's three OUTPUT values, and the blocker is no longer F12: the format spells the fold and components/age_distribution.esm evaluates it. It is F24 -- a document that ingests `data_sources` is forced onto the build-pipeline evaluation path, and that path resolves every causal self-read to zero silently. The upstream canonical valid example is the repro, and docs/findings/F24_control_a_recurrence_on_the_ingesting_path.esm is the one kept here.\n\nWHAT IT WILL PROVE ONCE THE PROVIDER IS WIRED: that each stage selects its own rows out of the real tables -- 55,471 emission rates, 62,699 population rows, 930,816 hourly temperatures -- rather than transcribing the handful its tests use; and that the roll-up can be diffed row by row against the 144-row MOVESOutput at the tolerances in tolerance.toml. Wiring it is a change of source for each relation's columns, not a change of shape: every component's joins already key on the columns these tables carry.\n\nTHE PRECISION THIS DOCUMENT IS EVALUATED IN, AND WHAT IT COSTS THE ASSERTIONS. `domain.element_type` is `Float32`, because `moves.rs`'s NONROAD port is `real*4` operation by operation and preserves the Fortran's associativity (docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §7.1). Nineteen variables override it back to `Float64`, and all nineteen hold an SCC: see `runSCC` for why, and note that the split costs no rewriting of a single expression, because every place an SCC meets a quantity in this document is a `join.on`, and esm-spec §11.3.1 makes a comparison hand its parent an exact 0/1 flag rather than a key (docs/esm-conventions.md §17).\n\nWhat the precision DOES cost is the assertion tolerances, and only some of them. The model default stays at `rel: 1e-12`, which is exact for every integer identifier a binary32 or binary64 evaluation can hold. Nine tests -- the ones whose every assertion is a floating-point QUANTITY -- override it to `1.1920929e-07`, which is 2^-23, one binary32 epsilon, the resolution of the declared element type. That is not a fitted number: it is the smallest tolerance under which a binary32 evaluation can agree with a decimal expected value at all. No expected value in this document changed; measured, the 39 assertions binary64 satisfied exactly and binary32 does not are spread from 1.2e-09 to 1.13e-07 relative, every one of them inside one epsilon.\n\nThe tolerance is per test rather than document-wide for the reason docs/findings F18 gives: `2260006912` is 4.1e-08 from `2260007005` and is a DIFFERENT EQUIPMENT CATEGORY, so a ten-digit key compared within one epsilon would pass while wrong -- which is precisely the failure this whole change exists to fix. The tests that pin an SCC, `run_fuelRegionID`, or any other key therefore stay at 1e-12 and remain exact, and `the_oxygen_content_survives_four_joins`, which pins both `run_fuelRegionID = 270000000` and a quantity, carries the loosened tolerance on the one quantity assertion instead of on the test. The loosening was also checked against what each test is built to discriminate; the tightest is `run_monthFraction`, where the table's 0.0833333 sits 4.0e-07 from the `defmth = 1/12` a missed lookup would deliver, a factor of 3.3 outside one epsilon.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "nonroad",
      "nr-logging-county",
      "source-catalog",
      "not-yet-consumed"
    ]
  },
  "domain": {
    "element_type": "Float32"
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "nr_logging_county_nremissionrate": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nremissionrate.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "SCC",
          "meanBaseRate"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nremissionrate"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "emission-factors"
        ],
        "note": "55,471 rows. Join J12 selects on (SCC via the equipment-chain fallback, engTechID, hpMin <= hpAvg <= hpMax, polProcessID in {101, 201, 301, 10001}); J13 takes polProcessID 9901 from the same table. SCC is utf8 in the file and becomes an integer key column in the document.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrdeterioration": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrdeterioration.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "DFCoefficient",
          "DFAgeExponent"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrdeterioration"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "emission-factors"
        ],
        "note": "424 rows. Join J14 on the composite key (polProcessID, engTechID). emissionCap is int64 in the file and needs no float_columns entry.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_zonemonthhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__zonemonthhour.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "temperature",
          "relHumidity",
          "heatIndex",
          "specificHumidity",
          "molWaterFraction"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_zonemonthhour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "meteorology"
        ],
        "note": "930,816 rows for the whole zone set. Joins J17/J18 restrict to zone 261610, monthID 8, hourID in [6, 18] -- 13 rows -- and average temperature over them. The most important entry here for the scaling gate: an unfiltered contraction against this table is the first place a non-driving join.on would stop being merely slow.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrsourceusetype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrsourceusetype.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "SCC",
          "medianLifeFullLoad",
          "hoursUsedPerYear",
          "loadFactor",
          "hpAvg"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrsourceusetype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "1,183 rows. Supplies hpAvg, loadFactor, hoursUsedPerYear and medianLifeFullLoad, which components/deteriorated_emission_rate.esm currently carries as parameter defaults. hpAvg is in horsepower, which the unit registry has no name for -- `hp` is not a recognised unit -- so it stays unitless in the document and the native unit lives in the variable description.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrscc": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrscc.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "SCC"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrscc"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "geography",
          "selection"
        ],
        "note": "214 rows, and no decimal column at all: SCC is a string key and NREquipTypeID and fuelTypeID are int64. Joins J1 (to nrequipmenttype) and J3 (to runspecfueltype) read it; components/geographic_allocation.esm transcribes six rows of it. Its fuelTypeID is the NONROAD namespace, where diesel is 23 and 24 -- the reason a RunSpec selecting onroad fuel 2 matches nothing (docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §5.4).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrequipmenttype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrequipmenttype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrequipmenttype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "geography",
          "selection"
        ],
        "note": "88 rows. The second hop of J1: equipment type to sectorID and surrogateID, which is the DB form of NONROAD's ALLOCATE.XRF. No decimal columns.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrstatesurrogate": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrstatesurrogate.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "surrogatequant"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrstatesurrogate"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "geography",
          "allocation"
        ],
        "note": "62,821 rows, the .ALO files. J6 takes the county row and the state row of one surrogate at the latest surrogateYearID <= the episode year and divides. surrogatequant is decimal text: without float_columns the allocation fraction is a division of two strings.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrbaseyearequippopulation": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrbaseyearequippopulation.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "population"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrbaseyearequippopulation"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "population"
        ],
        "note": "62,699 rows. J4/J5: the 1990 state population per source type. The value read here is NOT the value the engine uses -- nonroad_loader.rs:1226 rounds each row to one decimal first, because canonical writes the .POP file with %17.1f, and 0.463484 becoming 0.5 is a 7.9% change the snapshot cannot be matched without (components/equipment_population.esm).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrscrappagecurve": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrscrappagecurve.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "fractionLifeused",
          "percentageScrapped"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrscrappagecurve"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "population",
          "scrappage"
        ],
        "note": "197 rows, all NREquipTypeID 0 -- the default curve, the only one canonical writes, and a hard error if absent. NOTE THE CASING: the column is `fractionLifeused`, lowercase u, where docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §1.2 and every Fortran listing write fractionLifeUsed. Both columns are decimal text. components/age_distribution.esm carries all 197 points, because which breakpoint a life fraction lands on IS the computation.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "nr_logging_county_nrgrowthpatternfinder": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "file://${MOVES_SNAPSHOTS}/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__nrgrowthpatternfinder.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
